---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe1601.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — Applied Once Consolidation Is Elected" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Combining Financial Statements Line by Line" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Elimination of Intragroup Balances and Transactions" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Uniform Accounting Policies Across the Group" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Aligning Reporting Dates" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Loss of Control — Deconsolidation" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Labeling Requirements" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Eliminating an Intragroup Sale" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Worked Example — Deconsolidation Upon Loss of Control" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Relationship to IFRS 10's Consolidation Mechanics" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>





<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Combining a group's financial statements into one set of accounts</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 1601 governs HOW a PARENT enterprise, HAVING elected CONSOLIDATION under SECTION 1591, PREPARES consolidated FINANCIAL statements — COMBINING the PARENT'S and SUBSIDIARIES' individual FINANCIAL statements INTO a SINGLE, unified SET presenting the GROUP as ONE economic ENTITY. THE underlying MECHANICS closely PARALLEL IFRS 10'S OWN consolidation PROCEDURES internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Applied Once Consolidation Is Elected</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The implementation standard following Section 1591's policy choice</div><div class="principle">This Section applies to ENTERPRISES that HAVE elected, UNDER Section 1591, to CONSOLIDATE their SUBSIDIARIES — WHERE an ENTERPRISE instead ELECTS the COST or EQUITY method, THIS Section'S consolidation MECHANICS do NOT apply.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Combining Financial Statements Line by Line</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Assets, liabilities, income, and expenses added together</div><div class="text-supporting">CONSOLIDATED financial STATEMENTS combine the PARENT'S and EACH subsidiary'S assets, LIABILITIES, equity, INCOME, and EXPENSES ON a LINE-by-line basis — PRESENTING the GROUP as IF it WERE a SINGLE economic ENTITY, RATHER than a COLLECTION of LEGALLY separate COMPANIES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Elimination of Intragroup Balances and Transactions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Removing transactions within the group entirely</div><div class="text-supporting">INTRAGROUP balances, TRANSACTIONS, income, and EXPENSES (INCLUDING unrealized PROFITS and losses ARISING from intragroup TRANSACTIONS, such AS inventory sold BETWEEN group MEMBERS that REMAINS unsold at YEAR end) are ELIMINATED in FULL — ENSURING the GROUP'S consolidated RESULTS reflect ONLY transactions WITH parties OUTSIDE the group.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Uniform Accounting Policies Across the Group</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Adjusting subsidiary statements to match group policy</div><div class="text-supporting">CONSOLIDATED financial STATEMENTS are PREPARED using UNIFORM accounting POLICIES for LIKE transactions and EVENTS ACROSS the ENTIRE group — WHERE a SUBSIDIARY applies DIFFERENT accounting POLICIES from the GROUP'S own, APPROPRIATE adjustments ARE made to THAT subsidiary'S financial STATEMENTS when PREPARING the CONSOLIDATED statements.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Aligning Reporting Dates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Coterminous year-ends where practicable</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE PRACTICABLE, a SUBSIDIARY'S reporting DATE is ALIGNED with the PARENT'S own REPORTING date — WHERE this IS not PRACTICABLE, the SUBSIDIARY'S own MOST recent FINANCIAL statements are USED, WITH adjustments MADE for the EFFECTS of SIGNIFICANT transactions or EVENTS occurring IN the intervening PERIOD between the TWO reporting DATES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Loss of Control — Deconsolidation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Removing a former subsidiary's assets and liabilities</div><div class="text-supporting">UPON losing CONTROL of a SUBSIDIARY, the PARENT derecognizes the SUBSIDIARY'S assets (INCLUDING any GOODWILL) and LIABILITIES at THEIR carrying AMOUNTS as OF the date CONTROL is LOST, derecognizes the CARRYING amount of ANY non-CONTROLLING interest, and RECOGNIZES any RESULTING gain OR loss.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Labeling Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Every statement clearly identified as consolidated</div><div class="text-supporting">EACH primary FINANCIAL statement MUST be LABELED as "CONSOLIDATED" — CLEARLY signaling to READERS that the STATEMENTS present the GROUP as a WHOLE, RATHER than the PARENT'S own SEPARATE, non-CONSOLIDATED position.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Eliminating an Intragroup Sale</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Removing unrealized profit still sitting in inventory</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Unsold intragroup inventory</div><div class="wk-body">A parent sells inventory to its subsidiary for $500,000, recording a $120,000 profit on the sale. At year end, the subsidiary has resold none of this inventory to outside customers.</div><div class="wk-answer">The CONSOLIDATED financial STATEMENTS ELIMINATE the FULL $120,000 UNREALIZED profit — SINCE, from the GROUP'S perspective, NO sale to an OUTSIDE party has YET occurred — REDUCING both CONSOLIDATED revenue/PROFIT and the CARRYING amount OF the INVENTORY.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Deconsolidation Upon Loss of Control</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recognizing a gain or loss when a subsidiary is sold</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Selling a controlling stake</div><div class="wk-body">A parent sells its entire 80% controlling interest in a subsidiary for $3,200,000 cash. At the date control is lost, the subsidiary's net assets have a consolidated carrying amount of $2,700,000, with a related non-controlling interest carrying amount of $540,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The PARENT derecognizes the SUBSIDIARY'S $2,700,000 net ASSETS and the $540,000 non-CONTROLLING interest, RECOGNIZING a GAIN of $3,200,000 − ($2,700,000 − $540,000) = <strong>$1,040,000</strong> on DECONSOLIDATION.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 1601 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>List of significant subsidiaries, including proportion of ownership interest and voting power held</span><span>Basis of consolidation and any adjustments made for differing reporting dates</span><span>Nature and financial effect of any loss of control during the period</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether adjustments for a subsidiary's differing accounting policies or reporting date are genuinely necessary</span><span>Determining the exact date control is lost</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Amount of unrealized intragroup profit requiring elimination</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 10's Consolidation Mechanics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 1601 vs IFRS 10</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 1601</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 10</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Elimination of intragroup transactions</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Uniform accounting policies</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Whether consolidation is mandatory</span><span>NO — a Section 1591 policy choice</span><span>YES — mandatory for all controlled subsidiaries</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">ONCE consolidation IS elected, the MECHANICS are THOROUGHLY converged WITH IFRS 10 — the GENUINE divergence LIES entirely IN Section 1591'S own OPTIONALITY, NOT in HOW consolidation is PERFORMED once CHOSEN.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every consolidation event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Intragroup elimination</span><span>ALL consolidated statements</span><span>Removes transactions between group members</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Deconsolidation gain/loss</span><span><span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Recognized in the period control is lost</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1591</span><span>Subsidiaries — supplies the accounting policy choice determining whether this Section's consolidation mechanics apply at all</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1602</span><span>Non-controlling Interests — governs the presentation and measurement of NCI within these consolidated statements</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Intragroup elimination</div><div class="glossary-def">The removal of balances, transactions, and unrealized profits arising between members of a consolidated group.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Deconsolidation</div><div class="glossary-def">The derecognition of a former subsidiary's assets, liabilities, and non-controlling interest upon the parent's loss of control.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe1601 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
